  "prompt_text": "Use case: style-transfer. Transform the supplied deer sheet into another complete game animal sprite sheet, retaining the exact 2 rows by 5 columns, consistent scale, fine controlled sepia ink and restrained two-tone earth-colour washes. First image is layout/animal-style reference; person and scene are locked STYLE ONLY, never include their background. Actual transparent RGBA, no text, no labels, no grid, no ground, no shadow, no halo. Exactly TEN isolated whole figures with generous transparent gutters and margins, fully connected hooves/tail/horns. Top row SOUTH: front three-quarter 35degrees toward viewer LEFT from head-on, both chest and side visible. Lower row EAST: side three-quarter facing RIGHT. Same slightly elevated ~20degree camera, light upper left. Main contour twice interior line. Short hide: exactly3 small clusters of2-3 marks on shoulder/flank/haunch, diagonal upper-left to lower-right. Broad quiet washes, no all-over fur, not 3D or photorealism. Columns BOTH ROWS: 1 STAND,4 grounded hooves, alert; 2 WALK, obvious raised bent forehoof and opposite hind step; 3 RUN, airborne extended gallop, forelegs forward hindlegs back; 4 GRAZE, muzzle lowered completely to hoof level with bent neck, no grass; 5 DEAD, horizontal limp on side, legs sideways, eyes closed, no blood. Identical body size/proportions across upright poses. Designed to reduce to96x80frames; strong readable anatomy. SUBJECT: primitive wild HORSE, compact powerful dun/ochre body with darker dorsal stripe, dark brown short upright mane and full long tail, dark lower legs, single broad equine hooves, pale buff muzzle, strong rounded neck and long heavy horse head. Two short horse ears, no horns. Distinct stocky primitive horse anatomy, not a thin deer, no white blaze. Mane only3 groups of3 ink marks. Absolutely no tack, bridle, shoes, harness, saddle, accessories or rider. This horse is a pre-domestication wild source and later iron-age livestock by data.\n",
